From: peaches94 <peachescu94@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 26 Jun 2022 16:51:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Petal: Async Pathfinding

Fixed & Updated by KaiijuMC
Original license: GPLv3
Original project:  https://github.com/KaiijuMC/Kaiiju

Original license: GPLv3
Original project: https://github.com/Bloom-host/Petal

This patch was ported downstream from the Petal fork.

Makes most pathfinding-related work happen asynchronously

Imported into Kodama from Leaf (https://github.com/Winds-Studio/Leaf) @ becd099200691927e35a419c9534835db7bf8b31, patch 0040-Petal-Async-Pathfinding.patch.
Original license: GPLv3 (Petal, Kaiiju; stated in the patch header).
Kodama changes: Leaf's AsyncPathfinding config module replaced by async.pathfinding.* in kodama-global.yml read through dev.kodama.async.AsyncSettings; requests through the Paper Pathfinder API are always calculated synchronously; a failed calculation reports to the async-pathfinding FeatureGuard and yields an unreachable path; the vanilla profiler is only used on the sync path; the comment-only ShulkerBoxBlock hunk is not imported.

